models/sdreamer/
----------------

This directory contains a modified implementation of the sDREAMER sleep-staging
model. It is adapted from code developed by the model's original authors:

    Chen, J., Yao, Y., Anderson, M., Hauglund, N., Kjaerby, C., Untiet, V.,
    Nedergaard, M., & Luo, J. (2023). sDREAMER: Self-distilled
    Mixture-of-Modality-Experts Transformer for Automatic Sleep Staging.
    2023 IEEE International Conference on Digital Health (ICDH), 131-142.
    https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDH60066.2023.00028

That work was carried out at the University of Rochester under the NIH U19
BrainFlowZZZ research program (U19NS128613). Copyright in the original
implementation is held by the University of Rochester under its Intellectual
Property Policy, and the code is redistributed here under the MIT License in
keeping with the program's public code-availability requirement.

The model checkpoints loaded by this application are not the original authors'
weights. They were trained separately using the modified training pipeline at
https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/sdreamer_flow.


How to cite sDREAMER
--------------------

If you publish results produced by sDREAMER predictions, that is, scores
generated with SLEEP_SCORING_MODEL = "sdreamer", cite the paper above in
addition to this application. sDREAMER is separate work; citing this
application does not cite it.

BibTeX:

    @inproceedings{chen2023sdreamer,
      title     = {{sDREAMER}: Self-distilled Mixture-of-Modality-Experts Transformer for Automatic Sleep Staging},
      author    = {Chen, Jingyuan and Yao, Yuan and Anderson, Mie and Hauglund, Natalie and Kjaerby, Celia and Untiet, Verena and Nedergaard, Maiken and Luo, Jiebo},
      booktitle = {2023 IEEE International Conference on Digital Health (ICDH)},
      pages     = {131--142},
      year      = {2023},
      publisher = {IEEE},
      doi       = {10.1109/ICDH60066.2023.00028}
    }

Two points worth stating in a methods section:

  - The code under models/sdreamer/ is adapted from the original authors'
    implementation, not a verbatim copy.
  - The shipped checkpoints are not the original authors' weights, so reported
    accuracy will not necessarily match the published numbers.

The same citation is also carried machine-readably in the references: block of
CITATION.cff.
